{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-v2-0121-a", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "3.1 Evaluation approach", "locator": "3.1", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Our evaluations are intended to approximate the full capability that the adversary contemplated by our threat model could extract from the deployment candidate model, including by using the highest-capability tier of system settings, using a version of the model that has a negligible rate of safety-based refusals on our Tracked Category capability evaluations (which may require a separate model variant), and with the best presently-available scaffolds.", "paraphrase": "Evaluations are designed to approximate the maximum capability an adversary could extract, using top-tier settings, low-refusal model variants, and the best available scaffolding.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-v2-0121-b", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "3.1 Evaluation approach", "locator": "3.1", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "These measures are taken to approximate the high end of expected elicitation by threat actors attempting to misuse the model, and should be tailored depending on the level of expected access (e.g., doing finetuning if the weights will be released).", "paraphrase": "These elicitation measures approximate worst-case misuse and should be adapted to the anticipated level of access, such as finetuning if weights are released.", "modal_register": "conditional", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "OAI-PF-v2-0122", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "OpenAI", "framework_name": "Preparedness Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "3.1 Evaluation approach", "locator": "3.1", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Nonetheless, given the continuous progress in model scaffolding and elicitation techniques, we regard any one-time capability elicitation in a frontier model as a lower bound, rather than a ceiling, on capabilities that may emerge in real world use and misuse.", "paraphrase": "Because scaffolding and elicitation techniques keep improving, a single capability elicitation is treated as a floor, not a cap, on real-world capability.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
